        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: add GitHub Codespaces provider",
        "body": "Closes https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/348\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a direct GitHub Codespaces Linux SSH-lease provider with aliases `codespaces` and `gh-codespaces`.\n\n- Creates claim-owned GitHub Codespaces through the GitHub REST API and local `gh` authentication.\n- Uses `gh codespace ssh --config` to drive normal Crabbox SSH, rsync, `run`, `ssh`, `status`, `stop`, and cleanup flows.\n- Keeps the provider direct-only; it does not route through the Crabbox coordinator.\n- Adds provider config/flags/env handling, generated provider metadata, docs, OpenSSH config parsing, lifecycle tests, guarded standalone live-smoke coverage, and shared `scripts/live-smoke.sh` dispatch.\n- Keeps release and cleanup conservative: local claim required, creating login must match, dirty Codespaces fall back to stop/retain, and repo-local config cannot redirect creation to an arbitrary repository.\n\n## Verification\n\nLocal validation on current head `bcd0e9b255d88a105eb6ddabd79025e79b12bd2d` after rebasing onto the 0.34.1 development head:\n\n```text\ngo vet ./...\ngo test -race ./...\ngo test -race -count=3 ./internal/cli -run TestWindowsWSL2BootstrapCompleteProbeUsesWindowsMarker\ngo build -trimpath -o bin/crabbox ./cmd/crabbox\nbash -n scripts/live-smoke.sh scripts/live-github-codespaces-smoke.sh\nnode --test scripts/live-smoke.test.js scripts/live-github-codespaces-smoke.test.js\nnode scripts/check-command-docs.mjs\nnode scripts/check-provider-docs.mjs\nnode scripts/check-docs-links.mjs\nnode scripts/build-docs-site.mjs\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nThe full race run passed every package except the known load-sensitive WSL marker test timing out once; that exact test then passed three consecutive race runs. The live-smoke test suites passed 56 tests, docs checks covered 51 command docs, 70 providers, and 203 Markdown files, and whole-branch autoreview reported no actionable findings. The first rebased exact head passed every test but exposed core coverage at 89.8% against the 90.0% gate; this head adds focused coverage for the new Codespaces provider-default and explicit-override paths. Those race tests pass, the unrelated WSL marker test passes three consecutive race runs, focused autoreview is clean, and exact-head core coverage is now 90.3%.\n\nExact-head CI is terminal green: https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/actions/runs/28616544384\n\n## Remaining Merge Gate\n\nDo not merge yet while `status: 📣 needs proof`, `merge-risk: 🚨 auth-provider`, `merge-risk: 🚨 compatibility`, and `merge-risk: 🚨 security-boundary` remain. This still needs redacted authenticated GitHub Codespaces lifecycle proof:\n\n```text\nCRABBOX_LIVE=1 \\\nCRABBOX_LIVE_PROVIDERS=github-codespaces \\\nCRABBOX_GITHUB_CODESPACES_SMOKE_REPO=<owner/repo> \\\nGH_TOKEN=<token> \\\nscripts/live-smoke.sh\n```\n\nRequired proof should show `doctor`, create/wait for a short-lived Codespace lease, synced command execution, rendered SSH command, release/delete or safe stop/retain fallback, dry-run cleanup, final claim-owned inventory state, and no leaked token/output. The current local `gh` authorization lacks the required `codespace` scope, and the scoped 1Password metadata search found no matching Codespaces credential; live proof therefore remains the only blocker after exact-head CI.\n\n",
